  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Kostya brings champagne ordered to the room and assumes Chef Barinov is having a secret affair. Proudly promising male solidarity, Kostya vows to keep the secret—though Senya eyes the heavy bottle as a backup weapon.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Что случилось, Виктор Петрович?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Тут женщина шампанское в номер заказала.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Давай сюда и иди отсюда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Я понял, вы тут заняты.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, только никому не рассказывай.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Обижаете меня, Виктор Петрович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Мы же с вами мужики.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Мы настоящие хранители секретов.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Сегодня я вас тут прикрываю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Костя, быстро иди отсюда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Шеф, вы бутылочку не выбрасывайте.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Вдруг ещё кого-то оглушить придётся.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Что случилось, Виктор Петрович?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What happened, Viktor Petrovich?' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'what' and finishing on 'happened'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Тут женщина шампанское в номер заказала.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'A woman ordered champagne to the room here.' Notice how Russian expresses 'here' and 'to order' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Давай сюда и иди отсюда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Hand it here and get out of here.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'come on' and finishing on 'from here'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Я понял, вы тут заняты.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I understood, you are busy in here.' In Russian, the idea of 'I' flows naturally into 'busy' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, только никому не рассказывай.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, just do not tell anyone.' The negative particle sits right before the verb meaning 'tell' to negate the statement. Kostya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Обижаете меня, Виктор Петрович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You offend me, Viktor Petrovich.' Kostya brings out the contrast between 'insult' and 'me' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Мы же с вами мужики.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You and I are men, after all.' In Russian, the idea of 'we' flows naturally into 'lads' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Мы настоящие хранители секретов.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We are true keepers of secrets.' The grammar packs 'we' and 'secrets' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Сегодня я вас тут прикрываю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Today I am covering for you here.' Kostya anchors the line on 'tonight', while 'I cover for' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Костя, быстро иди отсюда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Kostya, get out of here quickly!' The grammar packs 'Kostya' and 'from here' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Шеф, вы бутылочку не выбрасывайте.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Chef, do not throw the bottle away.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'Chef Barinov' and finishing on 'to throw out'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Вдруг ещё кого-то оглушить придётся.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'In case we have to stun someone else.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'suddenly' before landing on 'it will be necessary'. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
